<p>We want everyone to be able to use the website and the app, including people with disabilities. The site was built against Israeli Standard 5568, which is based on the WCAG 2.1 guidelines at level AA.</p>

<h2>What was done on the site</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Language and text direction are set on every page: Hebrew right to left, English left to right.</li>
  <li>A "Skip to content" link at the start of every page, and a clear outline on whatever has keyboard focus.</li>
  <li>A "Reduce motion" button at the bottom of every page that stops the animations. The site also follows the device's reduce motion setting.</li>
  <li>The video at the top of the home page has a pause button and no sound.</li>
  <li>Text can be enlarged and zoomed, and pages don't break at the width of a small phone.</li>
  <li>Text contrast was measured against the actual background.</li>
</ul>
<p>In October 2026 every page of the site was scanned with the automated checker axe, at phone and desktop widths, and no violations of the standard were found.</p>

<h2>What hasn't been checked yet</h2>
<p>The site has not been audited by a certified accessibility professional, and has not been tested with every screen reader. There may be issues an automated scan doesn't catch. The app itself has not yet been checked against the standard. If you run into a problem, we'd like to know and fix it.</p>

<h2>Accessibility coordinator</h2>
<p>{{ site.author }}, <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. It helps to say which page the problem is on and what you were trying to do.</p>
